Job Title: Data Analyst Intern
&gt;
Department: Technical Staff
&gt;
Reports to: Lead Data Scientist, Soccer Analytics
&gt;
&gt;
Job Summary:
&gt;
As a Data Analyst Intern, you will assist the Lead Data Scientist, Soccer Analytics in various aspects of the role, including pre and post-game match reports, opposition analysis, and additional projects as needed. Your role will be instrumental in providing valuable insights and data-driven support to enhance team performance and decision-making. This position will work an average of 15 hours a week. There may be weekend, evenings, and holiday hours. This is a paid internship and college credit is available.
&gt;
Please note this position is allotted for the 2027 MLS Sprint Season, which runs from February through April. However, there may be an opportunity for continued employment during the 2027-2028 season based on organizational needs and individual performance.
&gt;
&gt;
What You&#x27;ll Do:
&gt;
Aggregate and process data for analysis of the overall quality of the game
&gt;
Analyze both event and tracking data for macro-level trends
&gt;
Produce compelling, illustrative and user-friendly (concise, informative) reports
&gt;
Provide support to existing and on-going projects
&gt;
Provide support across the entire soccer department, including ad hoc requests from coaches and other department directors
&gt;
&gt;
What You&#x27;ll Bring:
&gt;
Strong Analytical mindset and familiarity with data analysis tools including R and Python
&gt;
Experience working with Data Visualization tools including Tableau and PowerBI
&gt;
Familiarity and experience with all Microsoft Office Products
&gt;
Knowledge of databases, SQL and API&#x27;s to work with data from multiple sources
&gt;
Attention to detail, strong communication skills and ability to work in a team environment with a variety of stakeholders
&gt;
Good time management and organizational skills to keep up with a fast pace schedule
&gt;
&gt;
What You&#x27;ll Need:
&gt;
Pursuing Bachelor&#x27;s degree in Statistics, Mathematics, Data Science, Sports Science or a related…

AI Product Manager Intern
&gt;
About Astera Labs
&gt;
Astera Labs builds purpose-built connectivity solutions for rack-scale AI infrastructure. Our teams collaborate across functions to solve complex problems and deliver impact. As an intern, you&#x27;ll contribute to meaningful work alongside experienced colleagues and receive mentorship as you build practical skills.
&gt;
About the role
&gt;
Astera Labs&#x27; Applied AI team works to accelerate business outcomes through the use of AI as the company scales. We&#x27;re looking for a product-minded intern who can combine business judgment, user empathy, and hands-on execution. You&#x27;ll partner with cross-functional teams to discover high-value AI opportunities, define requirements, and help move selected solutions from concept to pilot and adoption.
&gt;
This role is intended for a candidate ready to take on broader product responsibilities than a typical implementation internship while remaining comfortable prototyping and testing solutions directly. You&#x27;ll work with stakeholders and technical partners to make trade-offs, define measurable outcomes, and ensure solutions address real user needs.
&gt;
What you&#x27;ll do
&gt;
Conduct stakeholder interviews and workflow discovery across business functions to understand user needs, pain points, and desired outcomes.
&gt;
Evaluate and prioritize AI product opportunities based on user value, business impact, feasibility, risk, and dependencies.
&gt;
Translate needs into clear product requirements, user stories, acceptance criteria, process flows, and a scoped pilot or MVP.
&gt;
Collaborate with engineering, IT, security, data, and business teams to align on solution design, dependencies, milestones, and decision points.
&gt;
Build or configure lightweight prototypes using AI tools such as Glean or Claude Code, and bring prototypes to users for feedback.
&gt;
Define success measures-such as adoption, quality, cycle time, time saved, user satisfaction, or risk reduction-and use results to recommend next steps.
&gt;
Help plan…

SG&amp;A AI Implementation Intern
&gt;
About Astera Labs
&gt;
Astera Labs builds purpose-built connectivity solutions for rack-scale AI infrastructure. Our teams collaborate across functions to solve complex problems and deliver impact. As an intern, you&#x27;ll contribute to meaningful work alongside experienced colleagues and receive mentorship as you build practical skills.
&gt;
About the role
&gt;
Astera Labs&#x27; Applied AI team works to accelerate business outcomes through the use of AI as the company scales. We&#x27;re looking for a curious, hands-on intern to help SG&amp;A teams identify and implement useful AI-enabled workflows. You&#x27;ll work directly with internal customers to understand how work gets done, break ambiguous problems into manageable steps, and build or configure practical solutions using tools such as Glean, Claude Code, and workflow-automation platforms.
&gt;
You don&#x27;t need to know every tool on day one. We&#x27;re looking for someone who has used AI tools in real work, coursework, or personal projects and can learn new platforms quickly, test ideas thoughtfully, and help people adopt what works.
&gt;
What you&#x27;ll do
&gt;
Meet with internal stakeholders across SG&amp;A functions to understand pain points, current processes, user needs, and constraints.
&gt;
Map workflows and identify opportunities where AI or automation can reduce repetitive effort, improve access to information, or make processes more consistent.
&gt;
Break larger opportunities into small, testable tasks; help scope pilots and define what success should look like.
&gt;
Build, configure, or prototype AI-enabled workflows using tools such as Glean, Claude Code, and approved automation or low-code platforms.
&gt;
Test solutions with users, review outputs for quality and reliability, capture feedback, and iterate.
&gt;
Document workflow designs, instructions, limitations, and handoff steps; help users understand and adopt the solutions.
&gt;
Track practical outcomes such as time saved, adoption, task completion, and user satisfaction.
&gt;
Follow…

SUMMARY
The Cybersecurity Governance, Risk Management &amp; Compliance (GRC) Intern will contribute to strengthening the security posture of a growing alternative investments firm. This opportunity is ideal for a curious, analytical, and collaborative individual who enjoys solving problems, simplifying complex information, and learning how cybersecurity enables business success.
&gt;
Working alongside the Cybersecurity &amp; Risk team, you&#x27;ll gain hands-on experience supporting governance initiatives, risk assessments, compliance activities, and security improvement projects. You&#x27;ll help translate technical requirements into practical guidance, research emerging risks and regulations, and collaborate with technology and business teams to support meaningful risk reduction.
&gt;
This 10-week summer internship is based in our Chicago office and follows a hybrid schedule, with in-office attendance required Tuesday through Thursday.
&gt;
RESPONSIBILITIES
The Cybersecurity Intern will support the Cybersecurity &amp; Risk team through the following activities:
&gt;
Apply strong writing and analytical skills to review, update, and simplify cybersecurity policies, standards, procedures, and controls aligned with frameworks such as NIST CSF and CIS Controls.
&gt;
Develop practical risk management skills by supporting security assessments, vendor reviews, client due diligence, audit evidence collection, and remediation tracking.
&gt;
Leverage curiosity, creativity, and problem-solving skills to identify and implement AI-driven solutions that automate manual GRC oversight activities, streamline workflows, and improve operational efficiency.
&gt;
Research emerging cybersecurity risks, regulatory requirements, and industry best practices. Strengthen critical thinking and communication skills by translating complex information into actionable insights and recommendations.
&gt;
Partner with technical and business teams to understand challenges, clarify requirements, and deliver meaningful process improvements…

At Relativity Space, we&#x27;re building rockets to serve today&#x27;s needs and tomorrow&#x27;s breakthroughs. Our Terran R vehicle will deliver customer payloads to orbit, meeting the growing demand for launch capacity. But that&#x27;s just the start. Achieving commercial success with Terran R will unlock new opportunities to advance science, exploration, and innovation, pioneering progress that reaches beyond the known.
&gt;
Joining Relativity means becoming part of something where autonomy, ownership, and impact exist at every level. Here, you&#x27;re not just executing tasks; you&#x27;re solving problems that haven&#x27;t been solved before, helping develop a rocket, a factory, and a business from the ground up. Whether you&#x27;re in propulsion, manufacturing, software, avionics, or a corporate function, you&#x27;ll collaborate across teams, shape decisions, and see your work come to life in record time. Relativity is a place where creativity and technical rigor go hand in hand, and your voice will help define the stories we&#x27;re writing together. Now is a unique moment in time where it&#x27;s early enough to leave your mark on the product, the process, and the culture, but far enough along that Terran R is tangible and picking up momentum. The most meaningful work of your career is waiting. Join us.
&gt;
&gt;
&gt;
About the Team:
&gt;
